Quick Start
Because this project runs purely on client-side JavaScript, no complex installation, backend server, or build step is required.

Prerequisites
To avoid CORS restrictions when loading local shapefile archives (.zip), run the file through a local HTTP web server rather than opening index.html directly via the file system (file://).

You can use any light static server:

Python 3: python -m http.server 8000

Node.js (npx): npx serve .

VS Code Extension: Live Server

Installation & Local Setup
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone [https://github.com/your-username/kultvis.git](https://github.com/your-username/kultvis.git)
cd kultvis
Ensure required static assets are present:
Verify that kulturverksamheter_utdrag_GBG_251212.zip and activities_bar_graph.png are in the project root alongside index.html.

Start a local web server:

Bash
# Using Python 3
python -m http.server 8000
Open in your browser:
Navigate to http://localhost:8000 to interact with the map.

How to Use
Toggle Data Layers: Use the legend in the bottom right corner to filter individual cultural categories, custom points, or visitor movement arcs on/off.

Toggle Section Collapsing: Click the headers in the legend or activity widget to collapse or expand panels.

Zoom Controls: Click the Global View icon to fit all active migration connections, or click the Close-up icon to immediately focus back on Lindholmen.

Inspect Attributes: Click on any building footprint, cultural site marker, or point of interest to reveal popup details.

